WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:02.750
A translation management system,

2
00:00:02.750 --> 00:00:07.418
or TMS, stores source content
and translations and runs the

3
00:00:07.418 --> 00:00:08.833
translation workflow.

4
00:00:09.233 --> 00:00:11.834
That workflow covers
translation memory,

5
00:00:11.834 --> 00:00:15.189
glossaries, review,
machine translation,

6
00:00:15.189 --> 00:00:16.395
and integrations.

7
00:00:17.150 --> 00:00:20.529
General Translation connects
translation generation and review

8
00:00:20.529 --> 00:00:21.735
to your code releases.

9
00:00:23.150 --> 00:00:26.447
Crowdin, Lokalise, Phrase,

10
00:00:26.447 --> 00:00:29.477
Smartling, and Transifex
are common examples.

11
00:00:30.150 --> 00:00:32.019
With General Translation,

12
00:00:32.019 --> 00:00:36.419
npx gt upload imports
existing translations,

13
00:00:36.419 --> 00:00:40.110
and npx gt translate reuses matches.

14
00:00:40.650 --> 00:00:44.551
A TMS still fits when language
vendors and CAT editors organize

15
00:00:44.551 --> 00:00:45.131
the work.
